\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CRIMINAL JUSTICE\par \par \uc2 U.K. Tech Entrepreneur Is Extradited to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Mike Lynch\uc2 , co-founder of U.K. software firm \uc2 Autonomy\uc2 , has been extradited to the United States to face criminal charges in a near decade-long legal battle and fall from grace for a man once hailed as Britain's answer to Bill Gates.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lynch, 57, faces 17 charges over \uc2 Hewlett-Packard\uc2 's $11 billion acquisition of Autonomy, the company he grew into Britain's leading tech company, before it spectacularly unraveled after the transaction in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Appearing in court on Thursday, Mr. Lynch, who could face 20 years in prison, was ordered by a judge to pay a $100 million bond, hand over his passport and to be placed under 24 hour guard to secure his release.\par \par \uc2 Once lauded by academics, scientists and politicians for setting up a software giant from his groundbreaking research at \uc2 Cambridge University\uc2 , he has spent the last decade fighting lawsuits related to the \uc2 HP\uc2  takeover.\par \par \uc2 The charges Mr. Lynch faces in the U.S. are for wire and securities fraud. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 LABOR\par \par \uc2 German Railway Union Plans 50-Hour Walk Out\par \par \uc2 A labor union representing more than 200,000 German railway workers said on Friday that it was going ahead with a planned strike next week after its demands for better pay were rejected by employers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EVG union\uc2  said its members will walk out for 50 hours from late Sunday until late Tuesday. The rail company \uc2 Deutsche Bahn\uc2  has canceled all long-distance travel during that period and warned that most regional trains also won't run.\par \par \uc2 The strike will likely be one of the biggest in recent years, following a previous large-scale walkout in April. But union co-leader \uc2 Cosima Ingenschay\uc2  said that a strike could still be averted at the last minute if employers put forward another offer.\par \par \uc2 EVG went into the current round of pay negotiations seeking a raise of 12 percent for its members, or at least 650 euros more each month. It also wants the minimum wage of 12 euros an hour to be ensured through basic pay rather than with bonuses, as is currently the case for some 2,700 workers.\par \par \uc2 The strike will affect dozens of rail companies as well as freight traffic. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 TAX INCENTIVES\par \par \uc2 Nevada Bill Would Bring Film Production to Vegas\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan group of Nevada lawmakers introduced a bill on Thursday that would give massive tax credits aimed at bringing film production to southern Nevada, including a $1 billion \uc2 Sony\uc2  expansion. It's the latest attempt at diversifying southern Nevada's gaming and tourism-reliant economy, which was hit hard by the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The $190 million in annual tax credits for 20 years would be the largest proposed tax incentive package in recent state history.\par \par \uc2 The legislation would involve the state entering an agreement with private developers who would pay for two film production sites.\par \par \uc2 ''It creates a whole new industry in Nevada,'' the bill's sponsor, State Sen. Roberta Lange of Las Vegas, a Democrat, said in an interview Thursday. ''I think it helps build and diversify our economy, which is something we've talked about in Nevada for as long as I've lived here.'' ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY CHRISTOF STACHE/A.F.P. -- GETTY IMAGES) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230513ej5d0004t\par }\page {\par\fs20